<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87416" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προερύω</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-έρυσσα</span> (v. infr.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>draw on</i> or <i>forward,</i>
			in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> always of ships, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆα θοὴν ἅλαδε προέρυσσεν</span>
			<i>drew</i> the swift ship <i>forward,</i> by hauling her from
			the beach to the sea, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.308
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπὴν ἅλαδε προερύσσω</span>
			(sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆας</span>) <i><span class="en">
				9.358
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>move</i> the ship <i>forward,</i> by rowing her towards the
			shore, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτὰς δ᾽ ἐσσυμένως προερύσσαμεν
					ἤπειρόνδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					9.73
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δ᾽ εἰς ὅρμον προέρυσσαν ἐρετμοῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.435
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.497
			</span></i> (but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προερεσσ-</span> was rightly
			written by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> and others).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
